WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.550
We have a song which we teach in class to help people remember the names of
the major dynasties.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.670
Right.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:20.050
It really does help to know which dynasty comes before which.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:24.340
So we're less concerned with the dates than we are with the chronological
order, the sequence of dynasties.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.430
Can you sing that song?
I cannot sing it as well as you can.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:28.620
[SPEAKING CHINESE: ni chang ba (please sing for us!)]

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.620
Well, shall we sing it together?

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.740
[SPEAKING CHINESE: ni chang ba (please sing for us!)]

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.060
Only if we sing it together.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:32.620
OK.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.340
[SINGING: Shang Zhou Qin Han, Shang Zhou Qin Han,

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.220
Sui Tang Song, Sui Tang
Song,

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.640
Yuan Ming Qing Republic, Yuan Ming Qing Republic,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.300
Mao Zedong, Mao Zedong...]

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.760
So if you sing this song once a day, you will always remember the sequence of Chinese dynasties.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.760
It works.
It's guaranteed.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.340
You will also drive your friends and family crazy.
It's true.

